{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Round 5 — design questions answered with data. (Q3) BLOCK→PASS flip attribution: 8% of all flips (31/404) happened with NO material change (pure flap); revised-material cited-text attribution is unrecoverable historically (SNAPSHOT compaction dropped old descriptions) — recommend recording cited-anchor hashes in the sidecar going forward. Staged re-review (re-run blocked criteria first) modeled NEGATIVE: 45% of re-reviews PASS and would each pay an extra serial stage-0 call; the mixed bucket (19%) converts one review into two author rounds; only the 13% persisting-only bucket wins — net ≈ break-even before latency, negative after. The DET cited-anchor pre-check captures the same win with zero LLM calls. (Q4) Overlap drain ROI: 0 of 2,093 plan reviews ever surfaced an overlap finding — the drain (~$165/5-days local + its failure storms) is not accomplishing its goal; recommend overlap_drain=off (config kill switch exists) pending redesign, or gate to ticket-creation only. (Q5) Cache TTL cliff CONFIRMED (read-share 68.7% at <5min gaps → 0.0% at >5min) but small: ~5% of consecutive calls are cold ≈ 2-3% recoverable — deprioritize. Analyses in reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786484751808672001,"uuid":"4eb6d662-43a7-4242-ad99-93de17cc54f1"}